# act (https://nektosact.com) — run the GitHub Actions workflow locally, in a
# container, as the clean-environment counterpart to .githooks/pre-push.
#
# The hook is fast and runs on every push, but against a warm tree: your
# node_modules, dist/ and Turbo cache are already there, so it cannot prove a
# fresh clone builds. act can — its `ts` job does `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# from scratch, which is exactly the check a warm local install hides.
#
# The workflow lives in .github/workflows-disabled/ (GitHub Actions is off for
# billing reasons, see commit 8acd5d4), so act has to be pointed at it — it does
# not scan that directory on its own. If CI is ever re-enabled and the file moves
# back to .github/workflows/, drop the -W line below.
-W .github/workflows-disabled/ci.yml

# Pinned explicitly so act never drops into its interactive "which image size?"
# prompt on a fresh machine.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run `pnpm ci:local` (act -j ts), not a bare `act`.
#
# A bare `act` runs EVERY job, and `wasm-drift` must not run here. Its self-heal
# step fires when the rebuilt artifact differs from the committed one AND the
# event is a push AND the actor is not github-actions[bot] — and under act, two
# of those three are true by default. The third is all but guaranteed: the
# workflow's own header states that identical rustc/wasm-pack/wasm-bindgen
# versions still produce different bytes on different hosts, and this repo's
# committed artifact was built on macOS while act runs Linux.
#
# With all three true the job runs `git add packages/compiler/wasm/`,
# `git commit` as github-actions[bot], and `git push origin HEAD:main`. The push
# fails without credentials, but under `act --bind` the commit can land in your
# real working tree.
#
# That job is built on the premise that CI is the canonical source of those
# bytes. Locally that premise is false, so the job does not just add nothing —
# it would assert something untrue. Staleness is already covered locally by
# packages/compiler/test/wasm-freshness.mjs, which hashes the Rust sources
# rather than comparing bytes.
#
# The `rust` job is safe to run (`act -j rust`) but pulls a full Rust toolchain
# into the container; it is cheaper as `cd crates && cargo test` on the host.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
